### dry-run as alice, without root: Enter
Firefox is installed as an Ubuntu snap.
G Unity⁷ provides a Firefox package with Unity's global menu:
  1) Install the G Unity⁷ package, copy the snap profile for alice and remove the snap (recommended)
  2) Keep the Ubuntu snap

Firefox and Thunderbird (7):
  Without root, the snap profiles of other users are not shown (sudo g-unity7-cleanup --dry-run shows them)
  Firefox: install firefox 159.0.1-1+gu7.1~26.10 from G Unity⁷
  Firefox: install firefox-l10n-cs 159.0.1-1+gu7.1~26.10 from G Unity⁷
  Firefox: install firefox-l10n-pt-br 159.0.1-1+gu7.1~26.10 from G Unity⁷
  Firefox: copy /home/alice/snap/firefox/common/.mozilla/firefox to /home/alice/.mozilla/firefox
  Firefox: remove the snap (snapd saves a snapshot of its data)
  Thunderbird: unchanged; the snap 160.0-1 is newer than the G Unity⁷ package 1:159.0-1+gu7.1~26.10, which could not open its profile. Run g-unity7-cleanup again after the package is updated.

